From b87fbda3d2b82ee94f9d7cd977047b5f2045ade4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LiBr <me@nvme0n1p.dev>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:17:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 49/57] Z 6III: the capture models from ../zr-qemu -- movie
 recording's chain and a Wave5 encoder

WonderLantern's zr-qemu (commit 8a00ced) records movies with a Nikon ZR's
own firmware on the same author's shared EXPEED 7 board that this tree
already carries at an older revision (../z9-qemu deb3a75). Its recording
chain is machine-type agnostic, so this is a re-import rather than new
devices: z63-tools/import_z9lab.py now reads ../zr-qemu, and
hw/arm/nikon-z63-z9lab.c is regenerated from it (still generated: edit the
script, not the file). The new overlay headers come with it --
nikon-expeed-{capture-pool,correction,dsp-boot,lossless,main-output,motion,
programmed-clock,video-preview}.h, nikon-z9-{source-ram,video-raw,wave5}.h,
nikon-wave5-codec.h, nikon-he-runtime.h.

Two of our own classes went away because upstream now implements them:
the second JPEG core (Ex7JPEGPort jpeg_ports[2]) and the d980 single-frame
relaxations (primary-d980-live-single-model); the attachment sets those
flags and wires their interrupts.

The Z 6III's H.265/H.264 block is a Chips&Media WAVE521C at 0x16010000,
the address the ZR model uses: Wave5VpuGetVersion (sub_40C53B34) and
ENC_PIC (sub_40C590EC) program it exactly as the model expects, and this
image polls 0x70 rather than taking SPI 88. The Wave5 model encodes with
the host's x265/x264, which hw/arm/meson.build now requires.
nikon-he-runtime-absent.c answers for the HE RAW coder, whose C++ archive
this tree does not carry; that model defaults off.

Two board hooks: the CPU release page (0x0d154000) asks the capture
models first, as every register window does -- a recording's start writes
its hold/release bundle, video reset, NR mask and peripheral select there
-- and -machine service-core-events=on wires zr-qemu's target/arm change
(WFE halts CPU3 until an SEV, cpu.h wl_event_*), off by default.

Movie recording itself is not reached on this body yet: see the import
script and the models for what each one asserts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
